  body: "# Choosing to suspend State Pension entitlement\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe SP chapter describes
    an option to suspend entitlement after entitlement has begun, and says that the person is not entitled during
    that elected period.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis voluntary entitlement option differs from administrative
    suspension of payment in chapter 4. The captured source limits exercise of the option, describes notice and
    cancellation rules, and compares overseas residence treatment with RP. Current legal applicability is unreviewed.\n\
    \n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 74503, PDF page 59](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=59).\n\
    - [DMG 74506, PDF page 59](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=59).\n\
    - [DMG 74529, PDF page 63](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=63).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch74` — PDF SHA-256 `5961a9cb7c86814a0f6fa147c0a8a551b4258c803680fac14a95cab9eca1afd6`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `c762e93940b4342d70d5bc96a80c3e094c91852d93868f5709e04f293faef61a`.\n"
