    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The option is explicitly an SP entitlement provision and is contrasted with RP overseas
      treatment in the source.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch74/0059
      quote: "74506 A person who has become entitled to a SP may opt to suspend their entitlement 1 in accordance\n\
        with DMG 74511 et seq. They are not entitled to SP for the period they have opted to suspend\n\nentitlement2
        and may not opt to suspend their entitlement more than once 3. The option to suspend\napplies to anyone
        claiming SP irrespective of where they live. This is different to RP where the option to\n“de-retire” or
        “elect to be treated as not entitled to a RP” is not available to people living overseas but not\nin an
        EEA country.\n\n\n                                                                 1 Pensions Act 14, s
        16(1); 2 s 16(2); 3 s 16(4)"
      locator: DMG 74506
